	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Lists the work that needs iTerm2 down (preferences waiting, a
claude-code upgrade, the Claude Peers workgroups) and runs it.

Return on a row runs ~/bin/iterm2-relaunch --yes with that item: it
ends every session in iTerm2, does the work, reopens iTerm2 and resumes
the Claude tabs. A heads-up with a "Not now" button comes first.

All logic lives in ~/bin/iterm2-relaunch - this workflow is two calls
into it, so there is nothing here to keep in sync. Alfred runs scripts
with /bin/zsh --no-rcs and a fixed PATH that excludes ~/bin, which is why
both scripts use an absolute $HOME/bin/iterm2-relaunch.

  irelaunch   list what is ready, hit return to run it
</string>
